d star Karen Dotrice of Mary Poppins (1964) fame. He and Michele produced one child, Emily. The subject of This Is Your Life (1955) on two separate occasions, the actor survived two major ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.imdb.com/search/name/?birth_year=1930\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d15\"},\"ref\":\"d15\",\"snippet\":\" ... decade before its time, prefiguring shows like The Office and Arrested Development with its lack of a laugh track, a single camera setup, and a roster of unlikable characters. It blurred the line between reality and TV show, with real-life actors playing themselves on the talk show ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.pastemagazine.com/tv/the-100-best-tv-sitcoms-of-all-time\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d16\"},\"ref\":\"d16\",\"snippet\":\" ... Dern appeared as real-life rancher George Spahn in Quentin Tarantino's 10-time Academy Award nominated \\\"Once Upon a Time in Hollywood.\\\" The film also won the Golden Globes & Critics Choice Awards for Best Picture, among others. He also co-starred in the #1 independent film of ... \",\"title\":\"https://m.imdb.com/search/name/?birth_year=1936&ref_=nmbio_bth_yr\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d17\"},\"ref\":\"d17\",\"snippet\":\" ... character Dr. Mark Sloan first in an episode of Jake and the Fatman, then in a series of TV movies on CBS that became the foundation for his popular television drama Diagnosis: Murder. The series ran from 1993 to 2001 with son Barry Van Dyke co-starring in ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dick_Van_Dyke\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"70456c23fd608727d28ad506906e13dfdd7a123544f547e804cfa2e7d77f53a0\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"08d473527ded3ce710214cc88aadcd7228db703e3493cf58a441f562d70adcdd\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"TV series character married multiple times only one child survives real life relative co-star\",\"view\":\"full\"},{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d18\"},\"ref\":\"d18\",\"snippet\":\" ... on Friends as fictional Days cast member Jessica Ashley (instead of her real-life series character, Sami Brady), Kristian Alfonso as Hope Brady, and Roark Critchlow as Mike Horton. In the Season 9 episode \\\"The One With The Soap Opera Party,\\\" in which Joey hosts a \\\"soap opera ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Days_of_Our_Lives\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d3\"},\"ref\":\"d3\",\"snippet\":\" ... Greif appeared on the science fiction show Blake's 7, which premiered in the late '70s, and more recently portrayed real-life politician Bernard Weatherill on season 4 of The Crown. His many other credits included the soap operas Coronation Street and Eastenders, the sitcom Citizen Smith, and ... \",\"title\":\"https://ew.com/celebrity/stars-we-lost-in-2022/?srsltid=AfmBOoqgtseDJPvB8Bamfe3oZlhWJZaiC5kf4fxP0pjffkBximQEpPNy\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d19\"},\"ref\":\"d19\",\"snippet\":\" ... The characters, costumes, and stories have changed, but the heart of the show remains.\\n\\n\\\"The Edge of Night\\\" (28 years)\\n\\nThe mystery soap opera focused on crime, rather than a familial drama like most soaps of the time. It aired from 1956 until 1984.\\n\\n\\\"Arthur\\\" (25 years)\\n\\nArthur ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.businessinsider.com/longest-running-tv-shows-all-time-2018-1\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d20\"},\"ref\":\"d20\",\"snippet\":\" ... Stars & Their Real-Life Romances\\n\\nAmanda Edwards / Getty Images / Rodin Eckenroth\\n\\nThe Young and the Restless remains the most-watched daytime soap opera on the air. Since 1983, Y&R has let viewers inside the lives of the captivating characters in Genoa City.\\n\\nMany of the soap's ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.swooon.com/gallery/young-and-the-restless-stars-real-life-relationships-couples-dating-history/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d21\"},\"ref\":\"d21\",\"snippet\":\" ... told Soap Opera Digest in 2022, adding with a laugh, \\\"I spent more time with a lot of these people than I have with my husband!\\\" Since 2007, Tom, who also played Kelly Cramer on One Life to Live, has brought to life Katie Logan on The Bold ... \",\"title\":\"https://soaps.sheknows.com/gallery/soap-stars-who-grew-up-on-screen/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d22\"},\"ref\":\"d22\",\"snippet\":\" ... starring on shows that ranged from McCloud (1970) to The Rockford Files (1974), from the miniseries North & South: Book 2, Love & War (1986) to the primetime drama Hunter (1976), co-starring Linda as secret agent Marty Shaw.\\n\\nAfter Dynasty, Linda decided there was something more to life than ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.imdb.com/search/name/?birth_year=1942-01-01,1942-12-31&gender=female\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d1\"},\"ref\":\"d1\",\"snippet\":\" ... Previous members have included Michael Rempel, Steve Clemens, Joel Jimenez, and Andy Parada. They have released more than a dozen studio and live albums.\\n\\nElizabeth Hubbard\\n\\nElizabeth Hubbard, the Daytime Emmy-winning soap opera star known for her roles on As the World Turns and The Doctors, died ... \",\"title\":\"https://ew.com/celebrity/stars-we-lost-in-2023-celebrity-deaths/?srsltid=AfmBOoquZ8XzskhVCclayEhMpQe5gv7r6Kz4o5tg6OyTyOQ4BYEBtxki\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d23\"},\"ref\":\"d23\",\"snippet\":\" ... several times more than their production costs. The issue's cover notably featured its first daytime soap stars, Bill Hayes and Susan Seaforth Hayes of Days of Our Lives, a married couple whose onscreen and real-life romance was widely covered by both the soap opera magazines and ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Soap_opera\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d24\"},\"ref\":\"d24\",\"snippet\":\" ... It seems that every time that she would have a real knockout year, another daytime diva would have a more unique story line, or a more challenging acting role, including multiple personalities, or an actress playing more than one character. But in 1999, on her 19th Emmy nomination ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.imdb.com/date/12-23/births\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d25\"},\"ref\":\"d25\",\"snippet\":\" ... In 1983, she divorced Motes, citing \\\"cruelty\\\"; she later said that marrying him was the biggest mistake of her life.\\n\\nCareer\\n\\nHe made his acting debut in 1974, appearing on the soap opera How to Survive a Marriage. He also appeared on the NBC daytime soap opera Another ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eric_Roberts\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"b350d1a34a0dd5191b05485e4e6da4f8ef2f50a4c8dac81f2c63e38cc5e821d0\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"d7c5aff6b7aed591ddd7a32b0a2aa6bd3b7bbec3e151dbf1130eb7a4916b14e1\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"soap opera character married more than twice one surviving child actor real life family member co-star\",\"view\":\"full\"}],\"search_raw\":{\"attempt_limit\":6,\"attempts_used\":1,\"document\":\"d1\",\"selection\":{\"block_truncated\":false,\"end\":117842,\"instruction\":\"Check the subject and adjoining context; lexical overlap does not establish the requested relation.\",\"matched\":true,\"matched_terms\":[\"actor\",\"65\",\"married\",\"series\"],\"method\":\"paragraph-lexical-v1\",\"score\":10.653329,\"selected_block\":[115442,116077],\"selection_is_semantic_support\":false,\"start\":114842},\"status\":\"success\",\"version\":\"search-raw-window-v1\"}}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_a32d5dd22b5b418882f1de55"},{"content":"The initial search didn't directly find the answer. Let me think about this more carefully. The clues point to a long-running series (more than 3 seasons as of 2023, started between 2000-2020). The \"character married more than 2 but less than 5 times\" and \"only one child survives\" are very specific. Let me search for specific shows and characters that match.","role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"queries\": [\"Grey's Anatomy character married three times one child survives\", \"character married four times one surviving child TV series\", \"actor plays with real life relative on TV show unrelated on screen\"], \"top_k\": 10}","name":"search"},"id":"call_6cd459f7bdbe454e9a91a0f5","index":0,"type":"function"}]},{"content":"{\"action_slot_charged\":true,\"executed\":true,\"ok\":true,\"raw_windows\":[{\"evidence\":{\"document\":\"d26\",\"document_chars\":9225,\"end\":3177,\"kind\":\"raw_evidence\",\"ref\":\"e2\",\"sha256\":\"ec7a971c1aba8708e9fecc437eaa4364c7b51bc1431a64a238ee58364cc9918a\",\"snapshot\":\"3c5ed9f149f8d9f24574ac5c50537c6ab9fab7b4f571a883113ea46f4a2cca81\",\"start\":177,\"text\":\"Evolution, fan comfort and a little TV magic have given these longest-running TV series staying power – sometimes for decades.\\n\\nIn 2024, there is no shortage of television programming to choose from. But quality series – those that have managed to captivate audiences season after season – are harder to come by.\\n\\nWhile certain TV series have been hits with audiences and critics alike only to be cancelled after one or a handful of seasons, (from My So-Called Life and Freaks and Geeks to Mindhunter), others just keep coming back. ABC's medical drama Grey's Anatomy is embarking on its 20th season, and the animated series Family Guy was renewed for its 23rd, appearing on Fox since 1999.\\n\\nThere's no exact formula for television longevity. Still, sticking around for decades means a show can reach millions of viewers not just at one time, but from one generation to another – a marker of a story and characters that truly resonate.\\n\\nHere are some of TV's longest-lasting shows that have managed to do just that.\\n\\nAnimated comedy: The Simpsons, 34 seasons\\n\\nThe Simpsons is one of the longest-running series in TV history. It began in 1987 as a short sketch on the Tracey Ullman Show before entering syndication two years later. And after an impressive 34 seasons, it's still being produced today. Few series have ever offered the kind of funny and cunning cultural critiques as The Simpsons – in fact, its writers have often been so spot-on with their commentary on current events, they've been credited with predicting them.\\n\\nSouth Park, which is slightly more political (and way less PG) than The Simpsons, seems to operate similarly. While it doesn't have quite as many seasons as Bart and family, the never-ageing trash-mouthed eight-year-olds of Southpark have been going strong on Comedy Central for 27 seasons and counting, still amassing plenty of viewers.\\n\\nChildren's television: Sesame Street, 54 seasons\\n\\nWe may not be able to tell you how to get to Sesame Street, but we can point you to the right channel: after 54 years, the programme still airs on PBS in the United States. Given that Sesame Street continues to educate children on the ABCs and kindness, while also featuring some of the most famous celebrities of any given era – from Robin Williams to Destiny's Child – it has good reason to keep going another half century.\\n\\nLate night: The Tonight Show, 70 seasons\\n\\nLate-night programming lends itself to cultural commentary like no other type of television. Perhaps that's why plenty of late-night shows, such as the sketch comedy series Saturday Night Live (now in its 49th season) and The Late Late Show (29 seasons) have stood the test of time. None, however, have lasted quite as long as The Tonight Show, which has seen six comedian hosts: Steve Allen, Jack Paar, Johnny Carson, Jay Leno, Conan O'Brien and the current host, Jimmy Fallon.\\n\\nMore like this:\\n\\n– Is the mediocre romcom making a grand return?\\n\\nSoap Opera: Coronation Street, 64 seasons\\n\\nNot all long-running sh\"},\"kind\":\"harness_acquired_raw_window\",\"previously_received\":false,\"selection\":{\"block_truncated\":false,\"end\":3177,\"instruction\":\"Check the subject and adjoining context; lexical overlap does not establish the requested relation.\",\"matched\":true,\"matched_terms\":[\"grey\",\"s\",\"anatomy\",\"one\"],\"method\":\"paragraph-lexical-v1\",\"score\":6.762885,\"selected_block\":[491,869],\"selection_is_semantic_support\":false,\"start\":177},\"source_document\":\"d26\",\"source_query_index\":0}],\"results\":[{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d26\"},\"ref\":\"d26\",\"snippet\":\" ... ABC's medical drama Grey's Anatomy is embarking on its 20th season, and the animated series Family Guy was renewed for its 23rd, appearing on Fox since 1999.\\n\\nThere's no exact formula for television longevity. Still, sticking around for decades means a show can reach millions ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.bbc.com/culture/article/20240318-longest-running-tv-shows-programmes-series-ever\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d27\"},\"ref\":\"d27\",\"snippet\":\" ... All the Times Meredith Grey Almost Died (or Suffered Another Trauma)\\nauthor: Dan Clarendon\\ndate: 2020-12-24\\n---\\nAll the Times Meredith Grey Almost Died (or Suffered Another Trauma)\\n\\nWe know there'd be no Grey's Anatomy without Meredith Grey … especially because creator Shonda Rhimes has said ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.tvinsider.com/979458/greys-anatomy-meredith-covid-near-death-traumas/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d28\"},\"ref\":\"d28\",\"snippet\":\" ... The incarnation was short-lived, with the block ending for the third time on September 27, 2019.\\n\\nHistory\\n\\nABC Friday-night legacy: 1950s to 1970s\\n\\nFamily-friendly comedies, which featured families with children as major characters, were a staple of ABC's programming dating back to the network ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/TGIF_(TV_programming_block)\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d29\"},\"ref\":\"d29\",\"snippet\":\" ... As the characters and universe of The Walking Dead live on in the new series, it's unlikely that the original show will be forgotten anytime soon.\\n\\n|\\n\\nTItle |\\n\\nRotten Tomatoes Critic Score |\\n\\nRotten Tomatoes Audience Score |\\n\\n|\\n\\nThe Walking Dead (2010–2022) |\\n\\n79% |\\n\\n78% |\\n\\n3 Grey's Anatomy (2005 ... \",\"title\":\"https://screenrant.com/tv-shows-ruled-world-airing-list/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d30\"},\"ref\":\"d30\",\"snippet\":\" ... MIKE HALE\\n\\nStream on Amazon.\\n\\n2005-present\\n\\nGrey's Anatomy\\n\\nBecause we all need our \\\"person.\\\"\\n\\nMore tears have been shed over \\\"Grey's Anatomy\\\" than any other prime time drama. It's been on longer than almost anything else, and it's also embraced tragedy, plucked heartstrings ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2019/arts/television/best-drama-series.html\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d31\"},\"ref\":\"d31\",\"snippet\":\" ... They married in 2014 and now share two children.\\n\\nPatrick Dempsey and Jillian Fink\\n\\nThe Grey's Anatomy star found his match at Fink's salon, Delux, in 1994. When the hairstylist noticed there was an appointment under the name \\\"Patrick Dempsey,\\\" she wrote it off as a ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.vogue.com/article/celebrities-married-to-normal-people\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d32\"},\"ref\":\"d32\",\"snippet\":\" ... Grey's Anatomy (2005–14)\\n\\nFrom 2005 to 2014, Oh played Dr. Cristina Yang in the ABC medical drama series Grey's Anatomy. Oh's portrayal of the pragmatic, ambitious Yang earned her five Primetime Emmy nominations for Best Supporting Actress in a Drama Series. She was one ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.thecanadianencyclopedia.ca/en/article/sandra-oh\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d33\"},\"ref\":\"d33\",\"snippet\":\" ... As with Grey's Anatomy and The Good Wife, the characters' relationships are just as important as their jobs.\\n\\n'Extraordinary Attorney Woo' (2022)\\n\\nWoo Young-woo (played by Park Eun-bin) is a young law prodigy, who graduated from the best school at the top of her class ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.marieclaire.com/culture/a26895105/best-korean-dramas/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d34\"},\"ref\":\"d34\",\"snippet\":\" ... He was previously married to Faye Grant and Marjorie Weinman.- Actress\\n\\n- Producer\\n\\n- Writer\\n\\nMulti-hyphenate actor, producer, writer, and director Sarah Drew is best known for her role as Dr. April Kepner on the hit ABC series Grey's Anatomy and as Hannah Rogers in Warner Bros' Everwood ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.imdb.com/date/10-01/births\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d35\"},\"ref\":\"d35\",\"snippet\":\" ... Grey's Anatomy superbly portrays the effect of losing patients and the importance of attending to one's physical and mental health. Characters in Grey's Anatomy and The Resident lose loved ones to COVID-19; in the latter, this loss is also tainted with the suspicion of ... \",\"title\":\"https://jamanetwork.com/journals/jama/fullarticle/2787497\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"p